// A validator for a SUBSET of CSS: it reads a declaration list, refuses
// everything it does not understand, and RE-EMITS what is left canonically.
//
// A LEAF. It imports `mizchi/css/token` and core, and nothing of tutuca's — not
// even `anode`, which is the parent of the directory it sits in. That is
// deliberate: `anode/sanitize` needs it for the `style` attribute, `vdom/filter`
// needs it for the same attribute at render time, and `tgc/policy` needs it
// for a guest's presentation attributes. None of those three imports the other
// two, so a validator that reached for any of them could only be used by one.
//
// Its own directory rather than a file in `anode/sanitize`, for the reason
// `vdom/filter/markup` gives for its: it drags a tokenizer behind it, and a
// host that only wants the name rules should not link one.
//
// Only `mizchi/css/token` is taken from `mizchi/css`. The parser package sits
// right beside it and is NOT used: `parse_inline_style` returns a layout
// engine's `@style.Style`, which cannot round-trip a declaration list, and
// round-tripping is the entire mechanism here. See `normalize.mbt` for the two
// places the tokenizer diverges from css-syntax-3 and what is done about them.
import {
  "mizchi/css/token",
  "moonbitlang/core/set",
}

import {
  "moonbitlang/core/set",
  "moonbitlang/core/test",
} for "test"
